From f06d2b35694a645e3aed7faa53af73999b6e30f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Youll <andrewyoull86@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 19:19:36 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 23/23] avformat: far seeks in a Matroska file with no index
 (Cues)

A Matroska file written without Cues has no index, and FFmpeg's demuxer
then seeks by reading every cluster from the start to the target (half of
the file for a seek to the middle: minutes from a network share, the
program frozen). A byte seek doesn't help: the demuxer ignores it.

mkv_index.c: before a seek with nothing in the index within 20 s before
the target, a cluster is found where the target should be (the file's
average rate; its ID, then any CRC-32, Void, Position or PrevSize, then
its Timecode), the guess moved until one is 12 to 42 s before the target,
and it's added to the index. The demuxer goes straight there and reads a
few seconds; the keyframes it reads are indexed as before. Used by
seek_video and seek_audio. A 600 s file: a seek to 56% read 1.2 MB, not
79 MB, with the same pictures as the indexed file, with or without its
Duration.
---
